#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:179
msgid ""
"Queries the UI layer at which a component is rendered, which can help in "
"determining when components occlude one another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:182
msgid ""
"The layer of a component indicates its relative stacking order with respect "
"to the onscreen visual representation of the UI. The layer index, in "
"combination with the component\\'s extents, can be used to compute the "
"visibility of all or part of a component. This is important in programmatic "
"determination of region-of-interest for magnification, and in flat screen "
"review models of the screen, as well as for other uses. Objects residing in "
"two of the Layer categories support further z-ordering information, with "
"respect to their peers in the same layer: namely, WINDOW and MDI. Relative "
"stacking order for other objects within the same layer is not available; the "
"recommended heuristic is first child paints first. In other words, assume "
"that the first siblings in the child list are subject to being overpainted "
"by later siblings if their bounds intersect. The order of layers, from "
"bottom to top, is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:197
msgid "0 - INVALID: Error condition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:199
msgid ""
"1 - BACKGROUND: Reserved for the desktop background; this is the bottom-most "
"layer, over which everything else is painted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:202
msgid ""
"2 - CANVAS: The \\'background\\' layer for most content renderers and UI "
"component containers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:205
msgid ""
"3 - WIDGET: The layer in which the majority of ordinary \\'foreground\\' "
"widgets reside."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:208
msgid ""
"4 - MDI: A special layer between CANVAS and WIDGET, in which the \\'pseudo-"
"windows\\' (e.g. the Multiple-Document Interface frames) reside. See the "
"GetMDIZOrder method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:212
msgid "5 - POPUP: Layer for popup window content, above WIDGET."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:214
msgid "6 - OVERLAY: The topmost layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:216
msgid ""
"7 - WINDOW: The layer in which a toplevel window background usually resides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:219
#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:237
#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:252
#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Component.md:269
msgid "unnamed_arg0"
